{"step_index":935,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-10T21:03:38Z","content":"Created At: 2026-11-11T05:03:38+08:00\nCompleted At: 2026-11-11T05:03:46+08:00\nCreated At: 2026-11-11T05:03:38+08:00\nCompleted At: 2026-11-11T05:03:46+08:00\nThe search for \"javascript-obfuscator options high obfuscation controlFlowFlattening deadCodeInjection stringArrayEncoding rc4 splitStrings\" returned the following summary:\nWhen configuring **`javascript-obfuscator`**[1] with a **high obfuscation** preset combined with options like `controlFlowFlattening`, `deadCodeInjection`, `stringArrayEncoding`, `rc4`, and `splitStrings`, you are employing a maximally aggressive security posture[2][3]. \n\nThe configuration below outlines how these options work together, what they do, and a sample JSON configuration.\n\n---\n\n### Breakdown of the Options\n\n1. **`optionsPreset: 'high-obfuscation'`**[4][3]\n   * **What it does:** Applies a pre-packaged suite of heavy-duty obfuscation settings[5]. It automatically turns on features like identifier mangling, string array extraction, and self-defending mechanisms[2].\n\n2. **`controlFlowFlattening: true`** & **`controlFlowFlatteningThreshold: 1`**[2]\n   * **What it does:** Transforms your JavaScript code structure by turning blocks of code into massive switch-case statements wrapped inside infinite loops. \n   * **The Threshold (`1`):** Means **100%** of applicable functions are flattened. This drastically hinders human readability and static analysis, though it carries a heavy runtime performance penalty[6].\n\n3. **`deadCodeInjection: true`** & **`deadCodeInjectionThreshold: 1`**[2]\n   * **What it does:** Randomly injects chunks of dead code (blocks that look like valid operational statements but are never executed) into the script[6]. \n   * **The Threshold (`1`):** Maximizes the volume of fake code injected, bloating the file size significantly and confusing reverse-engineers trying to trace execution paths.\n\n4. **`stringArray: true`** & **`stringArrayThreshold: 1`**[2]\n   * **What it does:** Extracts literal strings out of your functions and places them into a centralized array[7][8]. \n<truncated 2613 bytes>\nrKuHXBVSizbBvOlAEqFaH1vR3nGB6O2VIdpj7_EcdI0es4i_xlDmx8NxFI_p5wiNhje9za6roEFfylnjXhE8SzmuDXZvNB6uh9PQuRGGXrAe4aSt)\n[3] [github.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQG61tH33GF1sFHv5IQ0hO-hU4fZ8eorYE8JnGtLWDeqzntyis1w3vOIVg16eXR12IfoxHj4WzOrwiGbSO9ntSw5t3biyWBiw2vgS7qez1I6Ht1t11nTqxzRltt5HfevnY_Atn5VO5n9jYVTuWmBEStUQWeA8w-eiqx1QKAP1V0dvw==)\n[4] [github.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHYYHFiPnhMHsjKmZPJfdXEsGd5XxAXhoJHHfZg9-ch9UZHr4BX_KoNC1bMqst9xd74hTupSljGWgR8AAEYaAMOk-1gukaVmlXaA-tw0otgTcktKjc2jKlVZ6DzQZPdIAuTiYZKIrxBAkOwUaJmDlucVYaBFWvSWRBIT0O9OvltAaR07mvzK9gY)\n[5] [dev.to](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQE12ZVVizRuPneu6_cr11_x0LhntRFvXMO_09Q9xvMKTyTmXZvpnacTNJYChOBk617lwuAoTf4GAdsjd28tc0JA5zWwl1E88KMqFClq2TE93X7CMZVtCVu1AiKX4Gmbfede8KFOeKVlqljIX987Swf7Jtd4v-nfxfhclaY=)\n[6] [bytehide.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQF_fwIUvhE5bHPsPieOS2bEYN9Ac_UCshEsDBCq7P_Qm1p2aMUwnW9MiEWLgjJ2Rt0AA_EY4PvKs1SPoFalB0Y9qIkthTyv0lcphhHq0-1ZLeD3k2IPDg-jZkitZsYfUKx_4j3P6K0WB5HYTqz-WbbELWBl2ntv-BKbsu2cyYc=)\n[7] [npmjs.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQEdRkH3rkVOUaJYBBSF9sk9NOSZiHpfYZ35nvWkxJbt7-eiQCPanKJoXzOVn9EN_XrW4cqlBwWjjh7oQa7xSBbUWwYc2LiwS7fSaTU4c1gSZQZJQX-eMFiuSpH3B5z8Q9I2He9SpdWj1mI=)\n[8] [medium.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQE8LmorMdqv3rLaT99HLyz_2SVYlQqxRq6Ck1qwHyBDM6TSU3Dz0w7crlEwEzP8Z7mOiMhmoyOTIEXRZxTcVtPkxgTLYLZsoa54WEfb9x-D0EjEvf_Q1QKE5NX96nta5udSR_-cMvDex4LPscl2WyXpCHfCHWdbKOlhPAdlVAqvGnHq_q2AuYKSMGTrZv2kP08dgAAhHrbMlPRTBuholLYY3XrPhUsccZLGJKQR9zXktqoitg8N3dP3oSK7ymvsy5o=)\n[9] [npmjs.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.g