{"step_index":936,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-10T21:03:38Z","content":"Created At: 2026-11-11T05:03:38+08:00\nCompleted At: 2026-11-11T05:03:49+08:00\nCreated At: 2026-11-11T05:03:38+08:00\nCompleted At: 2026-11-11T05:03:49+08:00\nThe search for \"vercelignore syntax exclude folder files deployment\" returned the following summary:\nThe **`.vercelignore`** file is used to exclude specific files and folders from being uploaded and deployed to Vercel[1]. It follows the exact same syntax conventions as a standard `.gitignore` file[2].\n\n### 1. Where to place it\nPlace the `.vercelignore` file directly in the **root directory** of your project (the same level as your `package.json` or main configuration files)[2].\n\n---\n\n### 2. Basic Syntax Rules\n\n* **One rule per line:** Each file or directory pattern should be on its own line[2].\n* **Comments:** Use `#` at the beginning of a line to add comments.\n* **Folders:** Specifying a folder name will exclude that entire folder and everything inside it.\n* **Wildcards (`*`):** Match arbitrary characters.\n* **Negation (`!`):** Include a file that would otherwise be ignored by a broader rule.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Common Examples\n\n#### Excluding specific folders and files\nTo prevent folders like documentation, tests, or hidden draft files from uploading during deployment:\n```text\n# Ignore entire directories\n/docs/\n/tests/\n/private-assets/\n\n# Ignore specific file types anywhere in the project\n*.log\n.DS_Store\n\n# Ignore a specific file in the root\nsecret-config.json\n```\n\n#### Ignoring everything *except* what you specify (Allowlist approach)\nIf you want Vercel to ignore everything in your repository by default and only upload specific directories/files, you can use a wildcard combined with negation (`!`) rules[1]:\n\n```text\n# 1. Ignore everything in the root\n/*\n\n# 2. Explicitly allow only what is needed for deployment\n!api/\n!public/\n!src/\n!package.json\n!tsconfig.json\n!vercel.json\n```\n\n---\n\n### 4. Default Exclusions (No need to add these)\nVercel automatically ignores standard files and directories for security and optimization purposes (meaning you don't need to manually list them)[3]:\n* `.git`, `.svn`, `.hg`\n* `node_modules`\n* `.next`, `.vercel`\n* `.env.local`, `.env.*.local`[3]\n\nSources:\n[1] [vercel.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQG7doKZBfFC6397HMg5oWLkimd3W3beL2nJrCaT-B60QN2u0HFlppIHA_PniYvDN_mF4af87eZR-QH6NJwXpFsEGeOLjvHS9VKtewsSivZkdeYOWi8kTyBreTRvNPwQ5zWvXUk0MgQ=)\n[2] [vercel.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQG7doKZBfFC6397HMg5oWLkimd3W3beL2nJrCaT-B60QN2u0HFlppIHA_PniYvDN_mF4af87eZR-QH6NJwXpFsEGeOLjvHS9VKtewsSivZkdeYOWi8kTyBreTRvNPwQ5zWvXUk0MgQ=)\n[3] [vercel.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGsYnCV8BlQxENspoyBJVK2diuOKS4tBeE0yJJmKF7KRVc3TclwXtFkNoALlqh-QcVVMZEsLKz9kWFuhoAlYttJ2DsMXFCLos0FGo95KyIeM-nzOXXxPi3Sy7GfEREwH4Xcig==)\n\nNote: Source URLs are HTTP redirects; check where they resolve if you need the direct link."}
